items=[('Describe the changed ability.','Attention, episodic memory, executive control, mood, behavior, and independence require distinct observations and a timeline of change.'),('Compare complaints with performance.','Reported difficulty, direct testing, and family observations describe complementary aspects of functioning; sensory and motor prerequisites can change task responses.'),('Identify what the scan measures.','Structural MRI measures anatomy, diffusion MRI estimates water-motion properties, fMRI measures blood-oxygenation changes, and PET records tracer distribution.'),('Separate group results from diagnosis.','Average differences between former players and controls do not establish an accurate individual CTE test. Clinical syndrome criteria and confirmed tissue pathology are different standards.'),('Examine competing and coexisting conditions.','Alzheimer disease, Parkinson disease, depression, sleep disturbance, pain, and medication effects can contribute to symptoms in a former player.'),('Follow meaningful clinical outcomes.','Care can address symptoms and daily functioning while pathology remains uncertain. CTE-specific diagnostic and treatment claims require independent validation and appropriate clinical evidence.')]
